<BaseLayout title="About — SmartglassesBanned">
  <h1>About this project</h1>
  <p>
    SmartglassesBanned tracks real-world places, businesses, events, and jurisdictions that
    have restricted or banned smart glasses — devices like Meta's Ray-Ban Display that can
    record audio and video from frames that look like ordinary eyewear. Bans have been driven
    mostly by privacy concerns: covert filming in bars, changing rooms, casinos, and other
    spaces where recording isn't expected or welcome.
  </p>

  <h2>How entries are added</h2>
  <p>
    Every entry on this site is a Markdown file in the
    <code>src/content/bans/</code> directory of this project's git repository, each backed by
    a real news article. There's no automated scraping or user-submission form — entries are
    added manually, one file per ban, and reviewed like any other code change before merging.
  </p>

  <h2>Contributing</h2>
  <p>
    Found a smart glasses ban that's missing? Add a new Markdown file to
    <code>src/content/bans/</code> following the format of the existing entries (name,
    category, coordinates, source URL, and a short summary), then open a pull request.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
